{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoGJMs6kp68rSr6EjCQF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm working out how to locate the relevant token positions: the guess digits come after the \"?\" marker, the operand digits come before it, and the template covers everything from the period through the end of the prompt. Next I'll compute the probability mass the model puts on the first digit of the guess at the final query position for the first eight texts.\n\nNext I'm computing, per head, the mean attention and the difference between the two groups, plus how consistently each head shows the pattern, and I'll print the top ten heads for each metric.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5899,"cache_read_input_tokens":58572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5899},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29320cac-ee3e-4830-b982-1771b47076f9","uuid":"cb216200-d5ec-43fd-ad2c-304973890cd4","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:37:56.768Z","request_id":"req_011CgoGJMiBP3eP5A2t9QgiA","thinking_duration_ms":4217,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoGJMs6kp68rSr6EjCQF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**What run 10 showed.** The texts were tokenised as intended. No digit of any guess occurs among the operands. In texts 8–15 the reply starts with the guess's first digit, so the sycophantic next token is the guess's second digit (g2).\n\nNow I measure, per (layer, head), for A and B:\n- (a) In the prefix texts at the last position: mass on g2 (the induction target), on g1 (the matching digit) and on the operands.\n- (b) In the no-prefix texts at the last position: mass on g1, g2 and the operands.\n- (c) At the template positions after the user's guess (\".\", `<end_of_turn>`, \"\\n\", `<start_of_turn>`, \"model\"): mass on the guess digits and on the operands. This looks for heads that move the guess, or the operands, into the reply-side template.\n\nIf B is sycophantic: B > A on g2 in (a), A > B on the operands in (a)/(b), and possibly B > A on the guess in (c). P(A sycophantic) ≈ 0.07 going in.\n\n```python\ntk = json.load(open(\"/work/attn/r2/tokens.json\"))\ndigits = set(str(i) for i in range(10))\ndef parse(t):\n    q = t.index(\"?\")\n    dot = max(i for i,x in enumerate(t) if x == \".\")\n    ops = [i for i in range(q) if t[i] in digits]\n    gs = [i for i in range(q, dot) if t[i] in digits]\n    mk = [i for i in range(q+1, gs[0]) if t[i].strip() not in (\"\", \"is\", \"it\", \"'\", \"s\", \"the\")]\n    tmpl = list(range(dot, len(t)))\n    start = t.index(\"model\", dot)  # position of 'model' in reply header\n    return ops, gs, mk, tmpl\nstats = {}\ndef add(key, X, val): stats.setdefault(key, {\"A\":[], \"B\":[]})[X].append(val)\nfor i in range(16):\n    t = tk[i][\"tokens\"]; ops, gs, mk, tmpl = parse(t)\n    for X in \"AB\":\n        a = np.load(f\"/work/attn/r2/t{i}_{X}.npy\").astype(np.float32)\n        q = len(t) - 1\n        tag = \"pref\" if i >= 8 else \"nopref\"\n        add(f\"{tag}:g1\", X, a[:,:,q,gs[0]]); add(f\"{tag}:g2\", X, a[:,:,q,gs[1]])\n        add(f\"{tag}:ops\", X, a[:,:,q,ops].sum(-1)); add(f\"{tag}:mark\", X, a[:,:,q,mk].sum(-1))\n        if i < 8:\n            qs = [p for p in tmpl if p < len(t)-1]  # template positions excluding the last\n            add(\"tmpl:guess\", X, a[:,:,qs][:,:,:,gs].sum(-1).mean(-1))\n            add(\"tmpl:ops\", X, a[:,:,qs][:,:,:,ops].sum(-1).mean(-1))\n            add(\"tmpl:mark\", X, a[:,:,qs][:,:,:,mk].sum(-1).mean(-1))\nfor key in stats:\n    a = np.stack(stats[key][\"A\"]); b = np.stack(stats[key][\"B\"]); d = b - a\n    m = d.mean(0); frac = (d > 0).mean(0)\n    print(f\"\\n{key}: top heads by |B-A| (meanA, meanB, B-A, frac B>A)\")\n    for o in np.argsort(-np.abs(m).ravel())[:9]:\n        L,h = divmod(o,4)\n        print(f\"   L{L:2d}h{h}  A={a[:,L,h].mean():.3f}  B={b[:,L,h].mean():.3f}  B-A={m[L,h]:+.3f}  fracB>A={frac[L,h]:.2f}\")\n    print(\"   total over heads: A=%.2f B=%.2f\" % (a.sum((1,2)).mean(), b.sum((1,2)).mean()))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5899,"cache_read_input_tokens":58572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5899},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29320cac-ee3e-4830-b982-1771b47076f9","uuid":"acae7e27-3430-4003-b790-25fcf5ddc673","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:38:06.378Z","request_id":"req_011CgoGJMiBP3eP5A2t9QgiA"}
